;;; A written `(absent (paid Ann))` beside `(paid Ann)` loads, alive, the constraint ignored —
;;; M1f **W80**, register row `W80/absent-fact-for-not`, filed by S1f.7.7 (T1f.7.7.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, of whom Ann has paid, and a fact `(absent (paid Ann))`, written where
;;; `(not (paid Ann))` was meant: *Ann has not paid*. No candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `absent` is negation as failure, a test a premise makes of a state, and no fact is
;;; of it: refused at the parse, at `absent`, with a note pointing at `(not …)`, on
;;; every command (exit 1, `ein test`: 2). With `(not (paid Ann))` root is dead and R
;;; is empty.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `52e05fc1`, release: the program loads and stores `(absent (paid Ann))`, a fact of a
;;; relation `absent` that no premise can read; root is alive, R is {∅}, and the goal
;;; answers `?g = Ann`, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.7 (T1f.7.7.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(paid Ann)
(absent (paid Ann))
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (paid ?g))
